From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gustavo Noronha Silva <gustavo@noronha.dev.br>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 19:00:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] venus: track vn_ring_submit capacity in its own field
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

vn_ring_get_submit() matches recycled free-list nodes on shmem_count, but
the caller overwrites that field with the USED count after every submit —
the allocated capacity is lost the first time a node is reused with fewer
shmems than it was sized for. Nodes recorded below their capacity stop
matching larger requests, so every >=1-shmem submit scans the whole
(never-pruned) list and mallocs yet another node: unbounded list growth
plus O(n) per submit = quadratic CPU creep in long-running venus apps
(blobs demo: firefox 19.6% -> 29.3% CPU in 10 minutes at constant work).

Record the allocated capacity once, at malloc time, in its own field and
match on that; shmem_count goes back to meaning only the used count.

Upstream fixed this independently on main (09fb7ca8d82, MR !43229) after
this was authored; this release branch only carries the free-list scan
(d54c04f96c2), not the capacity tracking, so the bug is live here. Drop
this commit when the base moves to a tree containing 09fb7ca8d82.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/virtio/vulkan/vn_ring.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_ring.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_ring.c
index a0b39dcea53..01560841534 100644
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_ring.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_ring.c
@@ -72,6 +72,8 @@ struct vn_ring_submit {
 
    /* BOs to keep alive (TODO make sure shmems are pinned) */
    uint32_t shmem_count;
+   /* how many slots shmems[] was allocated with; never shrinks */
+   uint32_t shmem_capacity;
    struct vn_renderer_shmem *shmems[];
 };
 
@@ -437,16 +439,20 @@ vn_ring_get_submit(struct vn_ring *ring, uint32_t shmem_count)
 {
    list_for_each_entry_safe(struct vn_ring_submit, submit,
                             &ring->free_submits, head) {
-      if (submit->shmem_count >= shmem_count) {
+      if (submit->shmem_capacity >= shmem_count) {
          list_del(&submit->head);
          return submit;
       }
    }
 
    const uint32_t min_shmem_count = 2;
-   const size_t submit_size = offsetof(
-      struct vn_ring_submit, shmems[MAX2(shmem_count, min_shmem_count)]);
-   return malloc(submit_size);
+   const uint32_t shmem_capacity = MAX2(shmem_count, min_shmem_count);
+   const size_t submit_size =
+      offsetof(struct vn_ring_submit, shmems[shmem_capacity]);
+   struct vn_ring_submit *submit = malloc(submit_size);
+   if (submit)
+      submit->shmem_capacity = shmem_capacity;
+   return submit;
 }
 
 static VkResult
